<main class="content-page" id="main-content">
<header class="content-page-header"><h1>Editorial standards and corrections</h1><p>Useful guidance starts with clear explanations and honest limits.</p></header>
<section><h2>Sources and practical evidence</h2><p>Our publishing standard is to support factual claims with relevant sources, favor original documentation, and distinguish firsthand experience from research and opinion. Comparisons should explain their criteria and when information was checked.</p></section>
<section><h2>Authorship and illustrations</h2><p>Articles credit their author or the Bloogsite Editorial Team. Some contributors may use pseudonyms for privacy. Fictional About-page illustrations are editorial personas, not evidence of qualifications. We do not claim credentials or testing that we cannot support.</p></section>
<section><h2>Health and finance</h2><p>General educational information cannot replace advice suited to your circumstances. Articles should identify jurisdiction, limitations, and authoritative sources where relevant, and disclose any qualified professional review accurately.</p></section>
<section><h2>Corrections and updates</h2><p>If you spot an error, send the article URL, the disputed statement, and supporting evidence through a channel on our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. We review correction requests and aim to identify material corrections on the affected article. An updated date should represent a substantive revision.</p></section>
<section><h2>Commercial relationships and AI assistance</h2><p>Sponsored content and affiliate relationships should be clearly disclosed. AI assistance does not replace human responsibility for accuracy, sourcing, and final publication decisions.</p></section>
</main>
